# This repository stores DATA whose exact bytes are load-bearing, so git must
# never translate line endings on the way in or out.
#
# Two files make this concrete. `dataset/project_info.csv` is CRLF, and
# `official_fix.patch` for the CRLF-sourced projects (zip4j, hutool) must stay
# CRLF or `git apply` rejects it wholesale -- its context lines would match
# nothing. Worse, every official_fix.patch is hashed into its POV's
# certification `content_hash`, so a newline rewrite does not merely break an
# apply: it invalidates the certification, and the suite silently stops scoring.
#
# A checkout on a machine with core.autocrlf=input or true (a common default)
# would do exactly that. `-text` disables the conversion for every path.
* -text
